<title>ITALY: Toro reports higher premium income in 96.</title>
<headline>Toro reports higher premium income in 96.</headline>
<dateline>MILAN 1997-01-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Toro Assicurazioni, owned by Fiat, said on Monday that premium income rose 40 percent in 1996 to 3.7 trillion lire.</p>
<p>The company said in a statement that parent company premium income rose eight percent to 1.7 trillion lire, while premium income at Nuova Tirrena SpA, in which Toro acquired a 91.1 percent interest, was up 10 percent at 860 billion.</p>
<p>Group investments amounted to more than nine trillion lire with parent company investments up by more than 500 billion at 5.6 trillion.</p>
<p>-- Milan newsroom +392-66102321</p>
